        <briefdescription>
<para>Set previous error: cut <emphasis>prev</emphasis> from its previous &apos;tail&apos; of causes and link to the one <emphasis>e</emphasis> belongs to. </para>        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Note that all previous errors starting from <emphasis>prev-&gt;cause</emphasis> are transferred with it as well (i.e. causes for given error are not erased). For instance: e1 -&gt; e2 -&gt; NULL; e3 -&gt; e4 -&gt; NULL; e2:set_effect(e3): e1 -&gt; e2 -&gt; e3 -&gt; e4 -&gt; NULL</para><para><emphasis>effect</emphasis> can be NULL. To be used as ffi method in lua/error.lua.</para><para><parameterlist kind="retval"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>-1</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>in case adding <emphasis>effect</emphasis> results in list cycles; 0 otherwise. </para></parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
</para>        </detaileddescription>
